## 2. AGENT OUTPUT STREAMING

**Section 6.2 - Session Streaming:**

For the session stream view, we need to either:
1. **Read session event files** (`.kspec/sessions/{id}/events.jsonl`) via API polling
2. **Stream via WebSocket** — daemon publishes session events to topic

The daemon likely needs enhancement to support option 2 for true real-time streaming. In the interim, option 1 with polling (every 1-2s for active sessions) provides adequate UX.

**For dispatch agent output streaming:**
- Daemon captures stdout/stderr from spawned agents
- Publishes as `session:stream:{id}` WebSocket events
- UI subscribes to active session streams
- Falls back to event log polling if WS unavailable

**Section 4.5 - Session Stream View (Complete Wireframe):**

```
┌──────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ SESSION INFO     │ STREAM                                  │
│                  │                                         │
│ ID: 01KJX...    │ ┌─ Agent Message ──────────────────────┐│
│ Agent: worker   │ │ I'll start by reading the spec for   ││
│ Task: @task-auth│ │ the authentication feature...         ││
│ Started: 12m ago│ └──────────────────────────────────────┘│
│ Status: ● active│                                         │
│                  │ ┌─ Tool Call: Read ────────────────────┐│
│ CONTEXT         │ │ 📄 src/auth/login.ts                 ││
│ Spec: @user-auth│ │ Status: ✓ completed (0.3s)           ││
│ ACs to cover:   │ │ [▼ Show output]                      ││
│  ☐ AC-1         │ └──────────────────────────────────────┘│
│  ☐ AC-2         │                                         │
│  ☑ AC-3         │ ┌─ Agent Message ──────────────────────┐│
│                  │ │ Now I'll implement the token refresh ││
│ FILES CHANGED   │ │ logic based on AC-2...               ││
│ src/auth/login.ts│ └──────────────────────────────────────┘│
│ tests/auth.test.│                                         │
│                  │ ┌─ Tool Call: Edit ────────────────────┐│
│ BUDGET          │ │ ✏️  src/auth/token.ts                 ││
│ 1/3 tasks       │ │ Status: ● running...                 ││
│                  │ │ [Streaming diff...]                  ││
│                  │ └──────────────────────────────────────┘│
│                  │                                         │
│                  │ ┌─ Thinking ───────────────────────────┐│
│                  │ │ 💭 Considering edge cases for...     ││
│                  │ │ [▼ Expand reasoning]                 ││
│                  │ └──────────────────────────────────────┘│
└──────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Stream message types (from kynetic-internal's AggregatedMessage):**
- **Agent messages** — Markdown rendered, syntax highlighted code blocks
- **Tool calls** — Collapsible with icon per tool type, input/output, timing
- **Thinking blocks** — Collapsed by default, expandable
- **User messages** — If any (dispatch prompt context)

**Left sidebar context panel:**
- Session metadata
- Spec context with AC checklist (checked as agent covers them)
- Files changed during session
- Budget info
- Link to task detail

**Auto-scroll behavior:**
- Auto-scroll follows new content
- Pauses when user scrolls up (>100px from bottom)
- Resumes when scrolled back to bottom
- "Jump to bottom" floating button when paused

